          "committer": {
            "email": "noreply@github.com",
            "name": "GitHub",
            "username": "web-flow"
          },
          "distinct": true,
          "id": "8977443ecc1822db5e98d2a60462e0132f17dabe",
          "message": "chore(orchestration): reconcile bd-open beads against MERGED PRs (sq-13uyp) [OPUS-4.8] (#1082)\n\nAdd scripts/reconcile-merged-beads.sh: a per-tick maintenance sweep that closes\nthe gap where a bead's fix already MERGED but the bead was never `bd close`d, so it\nlingered on push-frontier.sh's launchable frontier and an agent was dispatched only\nto find the work done (sq-bpoey, merged via #1017, ~32k tokens wasted).\n\nIt COMPLEMENTS push-frontier's open-PR exclusion (sq-7mwun): that drops beads with an\nOPEN PR (in flight); this catches beads whose PR is already MERGED. For each OPEN bead\nit tests the merged blob (merged-PR titles + head-branches via `gh pr list --state\nmerged`, plus origin/main commit subjects) for the bead's EXACT dotted id token, with a\nboundary that excludes [A-Za-z0-9.] so `sq-ixc3.1` never matches `sq-ixc3.11` and a base\nid never matches a `.N` molecule.\n\nConservative + fail-safe:\n- DRY-RUN by default (report only); `--apply` closes matched non-gated beads with note\n  `reconcile: fix merged via #N`. Orchestrator reviews + applies separately.\n- OPEN/in_progress beads only.\n- NEVER auto-closes an epic (`issue_type==epic` or `[epic]`/`EPIC:` title), an\n  umbrella-parent (>=1 dependent), or a needs:user/needs:maintainer/decision bead —\n  those are reported for manual review.\n- Idempotent; a per-bead lookup error skips that bead (never mass-closes); an empty\n  merged signal (gh + git both unavailable) closes nothing.\n\nAlso:\n- scripts/tests/test_reconcile_merged_beads.sh — 32 hermetic end-to-end cases (stubbed\n  bd/gh/git) proving: merged-PR/commit match is flagged; open-PR-only + unrelated NOT\n  flagged; the `.1`-vs-`.11` false-match is avoided; epics/umbrella-parents/needs:user\n  are gated not auto-closed; --apply closes only non-gated candidates; idempotency;\n  fail-safe on no-signal + show-error.\n- AGENTS.md: wired into the maintenance-loop step-0 (run each tick) + the script catalog,\n  noting it complements sq-7mwun.\n- docs-quality.yml ci-scripts lane: shellcheck + both self-tests run HARD.\n\nEmpirical (dry-run over the current backlog): 9 close-candidates, 20 gated for manual\nreview. Both scripts are shellcheck-clean; self-test + harness green.\n\nCo-authored-by: Jesse Wright <jmwright.045@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
